    "No actual road add/remove, graph split, terrain cut/fill, junction rebuild, zonable regeneration, new zone painting or resulting lot generation was run. No product candidate was tested or rejected on a demonstrated physical-road failure.",
    "The source route adds only a global snapshot of shallow-copied authored node records. That is a diagnostic global write, not a world road/zone/building mutation. The existing planner still initializes the disposable page normally. debugEdge uses sampling/scratch state and freshly constructed spans, without regeneration or city edits.",
    "Current source/routed hashes and single marker were independently verified. No production code or saved user data was edited by this critic. There is no retained full before/after world invariant proving global purity across arbitrary future helper implementations.",
    "The clean official smoke was individually viewed:16 modules ready, zero errors,54.6FPS,430 draws,2061474 triangles,481.9MB raw heap. One accepted-source smoke is not a candidate visual comparison, sustained performance pass or forced-GC memory test.",
    "Props current source matches the declared accepted hash. The earlier transient import failure and isolated successful import are described by the builder; their complete incident logs are not supplied here. The fresh smoke proves current startup, not the exact cause of the earlier incident or a product repair.",
    "Only existing authored-node/cardinal pairs and currently painted/unclaimed frontage were screened. Mid-block splits, non-cardinal links, selective painting, modified sampling, coordinated block redesign and other local designs remain untested."
